    "category": "Mathematics - Chinese Remainder Theorem",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given two congruence equations: X \u2261 A (mod M) X \u2261 B (mod N) Determine whether they can be merged into a single congruence. If possible, output the merged congruence with the smallest non-negative solution.",
